1:["$","$Ld",null,{"page":{"id":"library--chorusing","kind":"library-article","route":"/roadmap/library/chorusing","sourceUrl":"https://refold.la/roadmap/library/chorusing","sourceHash":"6b475ac28edceea648291703228e029a0ed5ea174c62a5020e41d83488770976","collectedAt":"2026-09-01T16:52:39.063Z","bodyMode":"authorized-full-body","title":{"en":"Chorusing","zh":"跟声合唱法"},"description":{"en":"","zh":""},"segments":[{"id":"segment-0001","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Chorusing is a technique where you take a short audio clip (3-15 seconds) and repeat it over and over until you can say it just like the native speaker. It trains pronunciation, rhythm, intonation, and speech muscle memory all at once.","zh":"跟声合唱法是一种练习技巧：选取一段简短音频（3～15 秒），反复模仿，直到你能像母语者一样说出其中的内容。它能同时训练发音、节奏、语调和言语动作的肌肉记忆。"}},{"id":"why-it-works","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Why It Works","zh":"为什么有效"}},{"id":"segment-0003","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Chorusing is one of the most efficient ways to improve your speaking because it exercises multiple skills simultaneously:","zh":"跟声合唱法是提升口语效率最高的方法之一，因为它能同时锻炼多项技能："}},{"id":"segment-0004","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"<strong>Pronunciation:</strong> You're forced to produce the exact sounds the speaker uses","zh":"<strong>发音：</strong>你必须准确发出讲话者使用的每一个音"},{"en":"<strong>Prosody:</strong> You match the speaker's rhythm, stress, and intonation — not just their individual sounds","zh":"<strong>韵律：</strong>你需要模仿讲话者的节奏、重音和语调，而不只是单个语音"},{"en":"<strong>Speech muscles:</strong> Your mouth, tongue, and jaw get physical practice forming the sounds of the language","zh":"<strong>言语肌肉：</strong>你的嘴、舌头和下颌会得到实际练习，学会形成这门语言的各种语音"},{"en":"<strong>Listening:</strong> You develop a fine ear for the details of how the language sounds","zh":"<strong>听力：</strong>你会培养出敏锐的听觉，捕捉这门语言在声音上的细微之处"},{"en":"<strong>Chunks:</strong> You internalize common phrases and sentence patterns as ready-to-use units","zh":"<strong>语块：</strong>你会把常用短语和句型内化为可直接使用的整体单位"},{"en":"<strong>Self-monitoring:</strong> Because you're hearing the native model and your own voice simultaneously, you get immediate feedback on how close you are","zh":"<strong>自我监控：</strong>因为你会同时听到母语者的示范和自己的声音，所以能立即判断两者有多接近"}]},{"id":"tips","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Tips","zh":"技巧"}},{"id":"segment-0006","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"If you're struggling with a specific part, select just that section and loop it until you get it right, then go back to the full clip","zh":"如果某个部分让你感到困难，只选取那一段循环播放，直到能够正确模仿，再回到完整音频"},{"en":"If the audio is too fast, slow it down to ~85% speed. Once you can do it at that speed, bring it back up","zh":"如果音频太快，可以减速到约 85%。能够跟上这个速度后，再恢复原速"},{"en":"Start with shorter clips (3-5 seconds) and work up to longer ones","zh":"先从较短的音频片段（3～5 秒）开始，再逐渐挑战更长的片段"},{"en":"Chorusing is hard at first. The workflow feels awkward and the results feel slow. Stick with it — it gets easier and the payoff is significant","zh":"跟声合唱法刚开始很难。操作流程会让人觉得别扭，进步似乎也很缓慢。请坚持下去——练习会越来越容易，收获也会非常显著"},{"en":"Try writing down exactly what the speaker says (transcription) if you're struggling to hear the words","zh":"如果很难听清具体词语，可以尝试逐字写下讲话者所说的内容（转写）"}]},{"id":"what-you-need","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"What You Need","zh":"你需要准备什么"}},{"id":"segment-0008","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"en":"<strong>A chorusing tool:</strong> <ul><li><a href=\"https://chorusing.app/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">chorusing.app</a> Refold made tool with clipping and useful hotkeys <ul><li><a href=\"https://niallbunting.com/rechorus/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rechorus</a> is a simple web tool that also records and plays back your audio so you can listen to yourself. <em>Not affiliated with Refold in any way</em>.</li></ul></li><li><a href=\"https://chorusing.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">chorusing.com</a> Simple tool for basic chorusing with YouTube videos</li><li><a href=\"https://www.audacityteam.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Audacity</a> works too if you set up the right macros and workflows</li></ul>","zh":"<strong>跟声合唱工具：</strong> <ul><li><a href=\"https://chorusing.app/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">chorusing.app</a> Refold 制作的工具，提供片段截取功能和实用快捷键 <ul><li><a href=\"https://niallbunting.com/rechorus/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Rechorus</a> 是一款简单的网页工具，还能录制并回放你的音频，方便你听自己的声音。<em>与 Refold 没有任何关联</em>。</li></ul></li><li><a href=\"https://chorusing.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">chorusing.com</a> 一款使用 YouTube 视频进行基础跟声合唱练习的简单工具</li><li><a href=\"https://www.audacityteam.org/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Audacity</a> 也可以使用，但需要设置合适的宏和工作流程</li></ul>"},{"en":"<strong>Audio content:</strong> TV shows, podcasts, audiobooks, or pre-clipped sentence banks","zh":"<strong>音频内容：</strong>电视剧、播客、有声书或预先剪辑好的句子库"},{"en":"<strong>Headphones:</strong> But pull them slightly out or lower the volume when you're speaking so you can hear your own voice. You don't want to mask your output with the native speaker's audio","zh":"<strong>耳机：</strong>不过在开口说话时，请把耳机稍微移开一些或调低音量，以便听到自己的声音。不要让母语者的音频掩盖你的输出"},{"en":"<strong>Optional:</strong> a microphone with direct monitoring (pass-through) to hear your own voice more clearly in your ears","zh":"<strong>可选设备：</strong>带有直接监听（直通）功能的麦克风，让你能在耳机里更清楚地听到自己的声音"}]},{"id":"when-to-start","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"When to Start","zh":"何时开始"}},{"id":"segment-0012","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Chorusing works best once you have a base of listening comprehension in the language — you need to be able to understand (or nearly understand) what the speaker is saying.","zh":"当你已经具备一定的目标语言听力理解能力时，跟声合唱法效果最好——你需要能够理解或基本理解讲话者所说的内容。"}},{"id":"segment-0013","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"It's introduced as a secondary activity in Phase 3D and becomes a main activity in Phase 4A. It remains useful through Phase 7.","zh":"跟声合唱法会在阶段 3D 作为辅助活动引入，并在阶段 4A 成为主要活动。直到阶段 7，它都仍然很有用。"}},{"id":"research-and-reasoning","type":"heading","level":2,"content":{"en":"Research and Reasoning","zh":"研究与原理"}},{"id":"segment-0015","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"Chorusing as a formalized technique traces back to **Olle Kjellin** (MD, PhD), a Swedish scientist who published his prosody-and-perception method in 1998 in <a href=\"http://olle-kjellin.com/SpeechDoctor/ProcLP98.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">\"Accent Addition.\"</a> Kjellin's core insight was that pronunciation is fundamentally a motor skill, and like any motor skill (playing violin, surgery, typing), it requires massive deliberate repetition with immediate feedback. He reported striking results with his students — particularly immigrant professionals learning Swedish — though he acknowledged that controlled experimental validation had not yet been performed. His later paper <a href=\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/285234145_Quality_Practise_Pronunciation_With_Audacity_-_The_Best_Method\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">\"Quality Practise Pronunciation With Audacity\"</a> lays out the neurophysiological foundations and practical workflow in more detail.","zh":"作为一种系统化技巧，跟声合唱法可以追溯到瑞典科学家 **Olle Kjellin**（医学博士、哲学博士）。他于 1998 年在 <a href=\"http://olle-kjellin.com/SpeechDoctor/ProcLP98.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">《添加口音》</a>一文中发表了自己的韵律与感知训练法。Kjellin 的核心见解是：发音从根本上说是一项动作技能；与其他动作技能（演奏小提琴、做手术、打字）一样，它需要大量刻意重复，并获得即时反馈。他报告称，自己的学生取得了显著成效，尤其是学习瑞典语的移民专业人士；不过他也承认，当时尚未进行对照实验验证。他后来发表的论文 <a href=\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/285234145_Quality_Practise_Pronunciation_With_Audacity_-_The_Best_Method\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">《使用 Audacity 进行高质量发音练习》</a>更详细地阐述了这种方法的神经生理学基础和实际操作流程。"}},{"id":"segment-0016","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"The emphasis on prosody over individual sounds is well-supported by the broader SLA literature. Researchers in L2 pronunciation, have shown across decades of work that accent, comprehensibility, and intelligibility are related but partially independent dimensions — their <a href=\"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1111/j.1467-1770.1995.tb00963.x\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">landmark 1995 study</a> demonstrated that a speaker can have a strong foreign accent while still being perfectly intelligible. Crucially, their research found that prosodic errors (rhythm, stress, intonation) are a more potent force in reducing intelligibility than segmental errors (individual vowels and consonants), and that learners who received instruction focused on <a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1111/0023-8333.00047\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">global prosodic patterns showed greater improvement</a> in comprehensibility during free speech than those who received only segmental instruction.","zh":"第二语言习得领域更广泛的文献充分支持优先重视韵律而非单个语音。第二语言发音研究者经过数十年的研究表明，口音、易理解度和可懂度相互关联，但又是部分独立的维度——他们<a href=\"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1111/j.1467-1770.1995.tb00963.x\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">具有里程碑意义的 1995 年研究</a>证明，即使讲话者带有浓重的外国口音，其言语仍然完全可以被听懂。更关键的是，他们的研究发现，在降低可懂度方面，韵律错误（节奏、重音、语调）的影响比音段错误（单个元音和辅音）更大；而且在自由表达时，接受<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1111/0023-8333.00047\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">整体韵律模式训练的学习者在易理解度方面进步更大</a>，超过了只接受音段训练的学习者。"}},{"id":"segment-0017","type":"paragraph","content":{"en":"There is still no large-scale controlled study specifically testing chorusing as a standalone technique. The theoretical grounding is strong, the anecdotal evidence from practitioners is consistently positive, and the underlying principles (deliberate practice, prosody-first instruction, motor skill training) are each well-supported individually. But the specific combination hasn't been put through rigorous experimental evaluation yet.","zh":"目前仍没有大规模对照研究专门检验跟声合唱法作为独立技巧的效果。它拥有坚实的理论基础，实践者提供的经验性证据也一直相当积极；其底层原则（刻意练习、韵律优先教学、动作技能训练）也分别得到了充分支持。不过，这些原则的具体组合尚未经过严格的实验评估。"}}],"cards":[]},"siteBasePath":"/my_learning_docs"}]
